C. SEVERE AT 37,000 FT, AND THE INDEPENDENT READING OF IT
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SEVERE is drawn alongside 10^-5, and 37 kft is INSIDE
  that merge -- the two lines are one stroke of ink there. This project
  does not read a number out of a merge and call it one line, so:

     stroke at 37.00 kft       15.75 ft/s = 4.800 m/s   MERGED (SEVERE + 10^-5)
     -> sigma_severe(37 kft) = 15.7 +/- ~0.4 ft/s = 4.80 +/- ~0.12 m/s,
        the band set by which member of the pair the stroke belongs to.

  JSBSim FGWinds.cpp, the same figure transcribed independently,
  severe row interpolated 35k->45k:    15.82 ft/s = 4.822 m/s
  -> the two readings differ by 0.07 ft/s, 0.5%, which is inside the merge band.
     Neither set the other. An earlier pass here quoted 0.4% by reading
     the merged stroke as though it were SEVERE alone; that was too good.

  wind.mehta_residual_ceiling   = 4.459 m/s
  sigma_severe(37 kft)          = 4.800 m/s (+/- 0.12)
  -> `mil_f_8785c_sigma_w_exceeds_the_mehta_ceiling` points RIGHT, and the merge band
     is far too narrow to change that. IT IS NOT SETTLED HERE.

